WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.640
- So what inspired you to do this?

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.530
- I started walking across America

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:07.710
because I wanted to be
somebody I was proud of.

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.070
You know if somebody said
to me, who is your hero?

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:12.060
Or who inspires you?

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:14.810
I wanted to be able to look
them in the eye and say me.

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:16.907
I'm my hero.
(audience applauding)

00:00:16.907 --> 00:00:19.470
- Is it just like setting a goal

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.490
and finishing it and completing it?

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.020
- That's certainly part of it.
- Yeah.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.500
- You know out there you get
to have a no matter what clause

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.080
in that contract with yourself,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:32.240
because you do something like that,

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:34.540
and things can and will
definitely go wrong.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.134
- Yeah.
- Over that time period.

00:00:36.134 --> 00:00:38.830
- I heard you had a scary
incident that happened.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.340
- Yeah, when I was about not even halfway.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:44.850
I was in eastern Colorado, so
a very flat part of Colorado.

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.263
And I came out of our support vehicle

00:00:48.263 --> 00:00:51.207
and I got bit by a rattlesnake.

00:00:51.207 --> 00:00:52.040
(audience groaning)

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.705
- Which is deadly.

00:00:53.705 --> 00:00:56.370
- Yeah, if you don't get
to the hospital in time,

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.203
it could kill you.

00:00:57.203 --> 00:00:59.197
Most people survive.
- And you're probably

00:00:59.197 --> 00:01:00.410
in the middle of nowhere.

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:02.942
- I was definitively in the
middle of nowhere, yeah.

00:01:02.942 --> 00:01:04.200
(audience laughing)

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.540
Basically yeah, I was 30
miles from the last town,

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.884
about 60 miles from the next town.

00:01:08.884 --> 00:01:09.950
(audience groaning)

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.900
- [Kelly] Oh wow, look at the gnarly foot!

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:12.860
- Ooh.
- Oh!

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.690
- Oh my gosh.
- Yeah, so that was

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:16.340
a few days later.
- That's how my feet

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.636
looked when I was pregnant.

00:01:17.636 --> 00:01:18.890
(audience laughing)

00:01:18.890 --> 00:01:19.800
- That's real.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:22.880
I didn't have to walk
anywhere, it just happened.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.260
So how long did it take
you to recover from that?

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.000
- It took me about three weeks.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:32.000
So I went from doing 24
miles a day down to zero.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.650
So I just started building
my way up from the bathroom

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:36.690
and then they let me go home.

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:39.600
So I used the walker
to get to the kitchen.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:41.860
And then eventually I was
walking down the street.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:43.770
And then one mile, and two miles.

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.563
And--
- You picked it right back up.

00:01:45.563 --> 00:01:48.630
- I went, I had to go
back to the same spot

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.736
where I got bit to finish my journey.

00:01:51.736 --> 00:01:52.970
Because--
- Did you start

00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:53.932
with the middle finger?

00:01:53.932 --> 00:01:55.560
(audience laughing)

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.423
I would've.

00:01:56.423 --> 00:01:58.531
Been like, take that, snake!

00:01:58.531 --> 00:01:59.460
(audience laughing)

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.510
- I was actually pretty scared to go back.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.700
I didn't wanna go back there,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.040
but I knew I had made
this commitment to myself,

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:07.500
and like I said, I was doing that

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:09.520
to be somebody I was actually proud of.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:10.944
And somebody I was actually proud of,

00:02:10.944 --> 00:02:12.893
that person he doesn't quit.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:16.043
- How did it feel when
you got to Venice Beach?

00:02:16.043 --> 00:02:19.210
(audience applauding)

00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:21.300
First of all I'm gonna start walking

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.807
if I can get a waist like that, okay.

00:02:22.807 --> 00:02:25.963
Mama's gonna be walking
all day, all night, okay.

00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:28.570
How was it being on the beach?

00:02:28.570 --> 00:02:29.890
That was pretty cool, you finished it.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:31.160
You accomplished it.
- Yeah, it was definitely

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:34.200
one of the best moment
of my life, for sure,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.523
to make it there.
- Yeah.

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:37.870
- But at the same time,

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.370
even though I finished
my walk across America,

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.213
I'm not done.

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:46.740
I had an inkling before I left that

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.750
there was more inside me.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.040
And what I found out is
I was actually wrong.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:52.610
It's not just a little bit more,

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:54.370
it's like way more.

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:57.240
And so even though my walk is over,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.120
my journey is not.

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.330
And I'm not particularly
interested in becoming

00:03:03.589 --> 00:03:05.520
an old fat dude who says,

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.558
remember that one time
I did something cool?

00:03:07.558 --> 00:03:09.700
- (laughing) I love you.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:10.870
- I don't wanna be that guy.

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.060
I don't even really wanna meet that guy.

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:14.390
I have no interest in him.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:15.750
- You should make another album

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.374
and call it five million steps.

00:03:17.374 --> 00:03:19.774
(audience laughing)

00:03:19.774 --> 00:03:21.203
I'm just saying.

00:03:21.203 --> 00:03:22.036
- I'd download that.

00:03:22.036 --> 00:03:23.530
- Do y'all have something
that's huge like that

00:03:23.530 --> 00:03:25.529
on your bucket list?

00:03:25.529 --> 00:03:27.910
- Woo, my bucket list was to meet a man

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.180
who has walked 2,500 miles.

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.566
So I got that done.

00:03:31.566 --> 00:03:33.030
There you go.
- Check.

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:36.240
- Also to dance backup
one day for Beyonce.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.180
- Yeah!
- Yes.

00:03:37.180 --> 00:03:40.140
And I mean like, I don't mind
if it's all the way backed up,

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:41.240
like behind the curtain.
- Oh,

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.040
'cause you're a Houston girl, too?

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.020
B is too?
- Yes.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:45.440
- That's right.
- And I just wanna witness

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.216
those quads in person, that's all.

00:03:47.216 --> 00:03:48.049
(audience laughing)

00:03:48.049 --> 00:03:49.330
- I'm telling you, you tell
Beyonce get billions of views

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:50.460
you being in the next video.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.749
- I got you girl.
- Yes.

00:03:52.749 --> 00:03:55.493
I don't know if I'd want
to dance next to Beyonce.

00:03:56.343 --> 00:03:58.153
Unless it was a comedy.

